   "source": [
    "# Deal ya Doglapan? ‚Äî Workshop notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data Science Club √ó AWS Club ¬∑ Shark Tank India‚Äìstyle simulation**\n",
    "\n",
    "Open in Colab or a Jupyter-compatible editor, select a Python 3 kernel, and choose **Run all**. The supplied CSV is embedded. The notebook uses NumPy, pandas, matplotlib and scikit-learn (1.2 or newer).\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Part 1 ¬∑ Prathamesh:** inspect, clean and engineer 13 pitch-time inputs, then prepare the train/test handoff.\n",
    "- **Part 2 ¬∑ Parth:** run Logistic Regression together, then reveal the Random Forest and Gradient Boosting results.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workshop question:** Does a pitch end in a deal that the founder accepts? The 1,000 pitches and measured results come from a simulated dataset.",
    "\n\nThe interactive pitch desk is in **Stage 5**. Run all cells to try a pitch or download the offline dashboard."
   ]
  },
