   ],
   "source": [
    "rule = eda_train[\"Total Deal Amount\"].notna().astype(int)   # \"if a deal amount is written, predict Deal\"\n",
    "print(f\"Accuracy of this one-line rule: {(rule == eda_train['deal']).mean():.0%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1ceff292",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "üéâ **100% accurate!** Did we just solve Shark Tank?\n",
    "\n",
    "‚Ä¶No. `Total Deal Amount` is only written **after** the Sharks say yes. When a new founder walks in, it doesn't exist yet. Using it is like reading the answer key during the exam. This is called **data leakage**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The time-machine test:** *\"Would I know this column at the moment the founder starts pitching?\"* If not, it can't be an input."
   ]
  },
