   "source": [
    "implied = df[\"Original Ask Amount\"] / df[\"Original Offered Equity\"] * 100\n",
    "broken = (implied / df[\"Valuation Requested\"]).round(2) != 1\n",
    "print(\"Rows where valuation ‚â† ask √∑ equity √ó 100:\", broken.sum())\n",
    "df.loc[broken, [\"Startup Name\", \"Original Ask Amount\", \"Original Offered Equity\", \"Valuation Requested\"]]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "23d4c580",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Look at **ByteLabs**: an ask of **45,00,000** for 1.5% equity with a valuation of **3,000**. If the ask were **‚Çπ45 lakh**, then 45 √∑ 1.5 √ó 100 = **3,000** ‚úÖ. Someone typed the ask in **rupees** (45,00,000) instead of **lakh** (45). That's a **unit error**: the number is right, the unit is wrong.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same idea explains the others: a margin of **550%** is really **55%** typed with an extra zero."
   ]
  },
