  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c1f82125",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A few companies make **‚Çπ180‚Äì520 crore** a year. Are these errors too? ü§î **No!** Unlike a 550% margin, these numbers are *possible*: some big brands do come on the show. So we **keep** them.\n",
    "\n",
    "But they cause two problems:\n",
    "1. **The average lies.** One ‚Çπ520 Cr company drags the mean far above the median. It's like Ambani walking into a chai tapri: suddenly the \"average income\" in the room is in crores. The **median** (middle value) stays honest.\n",
    "2. **The chart is squashed.** Taking the **log** shrinks huge numbers: ‚Çπ10 L, ‚Çπ100 L and ‚Çπ1,000 L become evenly spaced. Now we can see the real shape.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Lesson 2: an error is fixed; a real outlier is kept and tamed with a log.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e9dfca5c",
