   "source": [
    "### Recap\n",
    "\n",
    "We defined the verdict, excluded outcome columns, repaired the simulated unit errors, built pitch-time features, and handed off the original split with an unfitted preprocessing recipe. Each model learns its own imputation, encoding and scaling inside its training pipeline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Part 2 ¬∑ Parth | Train your deal predictor\n",
    "\n",
    "| Minutes | What happens |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 0‚Äì3 | Ask the room to vote on a ‚Çπ50 lakh for 5% pitch. Explain Deal / No Deal and the Always Deal baseline. |\n",
    "| 3‚Äì9 | **Everyone runs Logistic Regression.** Explain the probability curve, then change the decision threshold once. |\n",
    "| 9‚Äì14 | **Facilitator reveals Random Forest and Gradient Boosting.** Explain voting and successive corrections with the pictures. |\n",
    "| 14‚Äì20 | Reveal the scorecard. Find the CV winner and ask the room to read two kinds of mistakes from its confusion matrix. |\n",
    "\n",
    "In a live session, start from the handoff with Part 1 already run. The facilitator can run the full notebook once ahead of time so the result figures are also available as saved outputs."
