  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stage 2 ¬∑ Run Logistic Regression together\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic Regression combines weighted clues and maps the score to a number between 0 and 1. The threshold turns that score into a verdict. Use one practice pitch from the training set to see those two steps."
   ],
   "id": "811f503a"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 26,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Business Services pitch | Ask: ‚Çπ250 lakh for 0.75% equity\n",
      "Practice-pitch deal probability: 84.7%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X_train, y_train = handoff[\"X_train\"], handoff[\"y_train\"]\n",
    "logistic = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"preprocess\", clone(handoff[\"preprocessor\"])),\n",
    "    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)),\n",
    "])\n",
    "logistic.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "practice_pitch = X_train.iloc[[0]]\n",
    "deal_probability = logistic.predict_proba(practice_pitch)[0, 1]\n",
    "pitch = clean.loc[practice_pitch.index[0]]\n",
    "print(f\"{pitch['Industry']} pitch | Ask: ‚Çπ{pitch['Original Ask Amount']:g} lakh \"\n",
    "      f\"for {pitch['Original Offered Equity']:g}% equity\")\n",
    "print(f\"Practice-pitch deal probability: {deal_probability:.1%}\")"
   ],
   "id": "6f4b8f91"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Student activity.** Set the threshold below the displayed probability and run the next cell. Set it above the probability and run it again. Discuss what changed. You used the same pitch and trained model both times."
   ],
   "id": "4eed21be"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 27,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Probability 84.7% | threshold 50% | verdict: Deal\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "threshold = 0.50  # Try a value below, then above, the displayed probability\n",
    "verdict = \"Deal\" if deal_probability >= threshold else \"No Deal\"\n",
    "print(f\"Probability {deal_probability:.1%} | threshold {threshold:.0%} | verdict: {verdict}\")"
   ],
   "id": "38b96f91"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stage 3 ¬∑ Reveal the two tree models\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Random Forest:** many trees see different samples and consider different clues. In the sketch they cast votes. In this implementation their class probabilities are averaged.\n",
    "- **Gradient Boosting:** trees are added one at a time to improve the current combined model. The running score can move up or down as a tree contributes a correction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The next cell is for the facilitator. Each model uses the same stratified five folds of the 800 training pitches. We select by mean CV F1 for **Deal**, which balances precision and recall. The standard 50% cutoff is used for the comparison, independent of the student activity."
   ],
   "id": "e5a24d8a"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 28,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Selected on training-fold Deal F1: Logistic Regression\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "seed = 42\n",
    "pipelines = {\n",
    "    \"Always Deal\": Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"preprocess\", clone(handoff[\"preprocessor\"])),\n",
    "        (\"model\", DummyClassifier(strategy=\"most_frequent\")),\n",
    "    ]),\n",
    "    \"Logistic Regression\": logistic,\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"preprocess\", clone(handoff[\"preprocessor\"])),\n",
    "        (\"model\", RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, min_samples_leaf=5, random_state=seed)),\n",
    "    ]),\n",
    "    \"Gradient Boosting\": Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"preprocess\", clone(handoff[\"preprocessor\"])),\n",
    "        (\"model\", GradientBoostingClassifier(max_depth=2, random_state=seed)),\n",
    "    ]),\n",
    "}\n",
    "folds = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=seed)\n",
    "training_rows = []\n",
    "for name, pipeline in pipelines.items():\n",
    "    scores = cross_validate(\n",
    "        pipeline, X_train, y_train, cv=folds,\n",
    "        scoring=(\"f1\", \"balanced_accuracy\", \"roc_auc\"), error_score=\"raise\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    training_rows.append({\n",
    "        \"Model\": name,\n",
    "        \"CV Deal F1\": scores[\"test_f1\"].mean(),\n",
    "        \"CV F1 Std\": scores[\"test_f1\"].std(),\n",
    "        \"CV Balanced Acc.\": scores[\"test_balanced_accuracy\"].mean(),\n",
    "        \"CV ROC AUC\": scores[\"test_roc_auc\"].mean(),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "training_scores = pd.DataFrame(training_rows).set_index(\"Model\")\n",
    "winner = training_scores.drop(index=\"Always Deal\")[\"CV Deal F1\"].idxmax()\n",
    "print(f\"Selected on training-fold Deal F1: {winner}\")"
   ],
   "id": "8ab97748"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Stage 4 ¬∑ Open the sealed test set\n",
    "\n",
    "**Accuracy** counts all correct verdicts. **Balanced accuracy** gives Deal and No Deal equal weight. **Deal F1** combines precision and recall for the Deal class. **ROC AUC** measures how well the scores rank Deal above No Deal across thresholds.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ask the room to identify a missed Deal and a predicted Deal that was actually No Deal. Read the counts from the confusion matrix. The held-out numbers measure performance on simulated pitches."
